 "title": "Adding up the present values of ever more payments",
 "caption": "Each payment is worth a little less than the one before, so the running total of present values levels off. Level £100 a year at 5% approaches £2,000; payments growing at 2% approach £3,333.33.",
 "alt": "Two rising curves over 100 years, each flattening: the level payments towards £2,000 and the growing payments towards £3,333.33.",
 "description": [
  "The present value of n payments of £100 at 5% is 100 × (1 − 1.05^−n)/0.05.",
  "As n grows this approaches 100/0.05 = £2,000.",
  "With 2% growth the limit is 100/(0.05 − 0.02) = £3,333.33."
 ],
